-# The DevTools Times
+# smallpt — The light lab
 
-This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
+Kevin Beason's original C++ smallpt renderer, compiled to WebAssembly and run locally in a dedicated browser Web Worker. The Astro home page is prerendered to `dist/client/index.html`.
 
+## Build
+
+Requires Node.js, pnpm, and Emscripten (`em++` on PATH).
 
 ```sh
-pnpm install && pnpm run start
+pnpm install
+pnpm build
 ```
 
-The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
+`build:wasm` compiles `native/smallpt.cpp` into the committed `public/wasm/smallpt.js` and `smallpt.wasm` assets. It also checks a small render directly against the compiled binary, including RGBA output and changed sphere colors. The adapter disables unused C++ exception support and reserves a 1 MB stack for recursive path tracing.
+
+## Browser behavior
+
+The original upstream reference image appears immediately. The browser then renders its own scene with progress and elapsed time. Randomize changes the mirror and glass spheres' RGB reflectance and starts a fresh render. Color pickers, samples, resolution, reset, and PNG download are available. Changing settings cancels the previous worker. No rendering service or cross-origin isolation headers are required.
+
+Source: https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/
 
-## Tech Stack
+`native/smallpt-original.cpp` preserves upstream source. `native/smallpt.cpp` retains the scene, intersections, and radiance integrator while replacing the command-line/PPM entrypoint with row-buffer and material-color exports. The upstream MIT license is in `native/LICENSE.txt`. `public/images/cornell-reference.png` is the upstream rendered result distributed with smallpt.
 
-- **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
-- **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
-- **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
-- **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+No preview server or browser verification was used.
